* START-HISTORY:
* 12 Sep 26 dm  The NO.QUERY @SDSYS skip leaves the DATA loop by "goto
*               more_test" rather than "continue", which re-ran "remove" on an
*               exhausted list and raised the 6135 prompt on an empty path
*               after NO.QUERY had already been honoured.  Measured, not read
*               (PORT_ADOPTION queue 22).  Same code at the port's DELETEF:246.
* 11 Sep 26 dm  Adopted from the Windows port: NO.QUERY takes the safe branch
*               in check.sdsys.file (msg 10117, port PRE_RELEASE 14, UPSTREAM
*               23); the DATA/DICT path comparisons ignore case (port 26,
*               UPSTREAM 27); the banned-file guard upcases the name; both
*               relocated-index deletes are checked, and only when the
*               directory exists (msg 2636, port 104 and 113, UPSTREAM 34).
*               NOT taken: the port's open 'voc' - lower case is section M.
*               Linux addition: the DATA/DICT prompts and 6131 "Use file"
*               show their default and Enter is N, as port 79 requires of
*               every prompt - these
*               were missed there, and at end of input they re-asked for ever
*               (98.9 MB in 40 s, measured 11 Sep 2026 down a pipe).
* 10 Sep 26 dm  Parity audit: Enter is N at the system-account prompt (port
*               PRE_RELEASE_FIXES 79).
* 19 Jan 04  0.6.1 SD launch. Earlier history details suppressed.
* END-HISTORY
